      "content": "I recognize the urgency in addressing the high cost of inference within the reason modules. To explore the viability of transitioning to a script-based automation system, we should start by cataloging all current tasks handled by the DevOps Agent and identify commonalities that can be converted into efficient Bash or Python scripts. We’ll want to look at lighter versions of scripts capable of monitoring resource usage and managing deployments with minimal overhead. Alongside this, a cost-benefit analysis comparing the reduced expenses against potential downgrades in functionality and performance will be critical to evaluate the risks associated with such a switch. This analysis will enable us to explore whether it's more cost-effective in the long run to maintain the current setup versus optimizing the existing infrastructure versus shifting to a simpler scripted approach that may lead to a loss in automation benefits. It is also essential to ensure that any new scripts we develop are future-proof and will continue to meet our evolving needs.",
